

SocialMedia Backend (Spring Boot)

A backend service for a Social Media application built with Spring Boot. This project provides RESTful APIs for managing users, posts, comments, and interactions, designed with scalability and modularity in mind.

---

📌 Features
- User Management: Register, login, and manage user profiles.
- Post APIs: Create, update, delete, and fetch posts.
- Comment APIs: Add and manage comments on posts.
- Like System: Like/unlike posts and track engagement.
- Spring Boot Architecture: Built with controllers, services, and repositories for clean separation of concerns.
- RESTful APIs: JSON-based endpoints for easy integration with frontend apps.

---

📂 Project Structure
`
SocialMedia/
 └── Backend/
      ├── src/main/java/com/socialmedia/
      │    ├── controller/   # REST controllers
      │    ├── service/      # Business logic
      │    ├── repository/   # Data access layer
      │    └── model/        # Entities (User, Post, Comment)
      └── src/main/resources/
           └── application.properties
`

---

⚙️ Requirements
- Java 17+
- Spring Boot 3.x
- Maven/Gradle
- Database: H2 (default) or MySQL/PostgreSQL (configurable)